  "id": "B07SYTRPSG",
  "notes": [
    "Grinder type: As an electric blade grinder, it uses a high-speed dual stainless steel blade to chop beans and dry ingredients rather than crushing them like a burr grinder, offering a compact, fast, and versatile tool for both coffee and whole spices.",
    "Power and batch capacity: Driven by a 150-watt motor, the grinding bowl holds up to 30 grams (approximately 1 ounce) of whole beans per cycle, yielding enough freshly ground coffee for 4 to 6 standard cups of drip coffee.",
    "Texture control via pulsing: Because blade grinders lack fixed click-settings, particle size is controlled by grind time; pulsing in short 2- to 3-second bursts—and giving the unit a light shake between pulses—helps achieve a more uniform particle size and prevents heat buildup from scorching delicate coffee oils.",
    "Brewing compatibility: Performs best for automatic drip makers, pour-over cones, and French press coffee; it is generally not recommended for espresso, which requires the ultra-fine, uniform calibration of a dedicated burr grinder.",
    "Cleaning and maintenance: Clean the grinding chamber using a soft brush or a dry cloth (the motorized base should never be submerged in water); pulsing a tablespoon of dry, uncooked white rice through the chamber periodically will absorb stale coffee oils and clear lingering aromas between switching from spices to coffee."
  ],
